
#import "../../../_lib/kodama.typ": *

#show: kodama

#metadata((
  title: "δ-rings",
))

#subtree(
  title: "Definition of δ-rings",
  taxon: "section"
)[
A $delta$-ring is a is a commutative ring $R$ equipped with $delta : R -> R$ such that:
$
  delta(0) & = 0 \
  delta(1) & = 0 \
  delta(x y) & = x^p delta(y) + y^p delta(x) + p delta(x) delta(y) \
  delta(x + y) & = delta(x) + delta(y) + p^(-1)(x^p + y^p - (x + y)^p)
$
#subtree(
  taxon: [Remark]
)[
  Given any $delta$-ring $R$, we construct the associated Frobenius lift:
  $
    phi(x) & := x^p + p delta(x)
  $
  Then $phi$ is a ring homomorphism that lifts Frobenius on $R times.o_ZZ FF_p$. Converse make sense if $R$ is $p$-torsion free. In particular, if $R$ is over $QQ$, then a $delta$-ring is just a ring with endomorphism $phi$.
]
Recall the theory of #local("trees/wiki/p-adic/Prismatic/Witt.typst").
#subtree(
  taxon: [Remark]
)[
  A $delta$-ring structure on $R$ is exactly a section of the projection $W_2(R) -> R$.
]

#subtree(
  taxon: [Remark]
)[
  Recall in #local("trees/wiki/p-adic/Prismatic/Witt.typst"),
]
]
